[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3391170164","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111020#issuecomment-3391170164","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111020","id":3391170164,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7KISZ0","user":{"login":"xuhuisheng","id":1118508,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMTg1MDg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1118508?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng","html_url":"https://github.com/xuhuisheng","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-10T16:48:10Z","updated_at":"2025-10-10T16:48:10Z","body":"Hi @mh114 ,\n\nI did some investigations, e.g. sync `instance_shade_parameters` from `CanvasItem` to `TileMapLayer` scope, but it is not easy to achieve the goal. While, It seems didn't get benefit from `TileMapLayer`, e.g. Tiles.\n\nLooks like `TileMapLayer` create an individual CID for rendering, and it can use material of `CanvasItem` as parent material. That makes material and instance_shade_parameters coming from different scopes, one from `CanvasItem`, the other from `TileMayLayer`. That is why `offset` works, because `offset` will set to material directly, which comes from the same scope, `CanvasItem`.\n\nAs above information, I try to sync data from `CanvasItem` to `TileMapLayer`, but they have different refresh period. `TileMapLayer` didn't trigger re-render, if the tiles didn't update. So I didn't find a good point to trigger refresh, yet. And that makes we cannot use traditional Tile on the `TileMap`. Maybe I am mis-understanding this, but it cannot implement multiple layers in one `TileMapLayer`.\n\nSo, my suggestion is using other Node type to replacing `TileMapLayer`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3391170164/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3391488673","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111020#issuecomment-3391488673","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111020","id":3391488673,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7KJgKh","user":{"login":"mh114","id":149063404,"node_id":"U_kgDOCOKG7A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/149063404?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mh114","html_url":"https://github.com/mh114","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mh114/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mh114/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mh114/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mh114/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mh114/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mh114/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mh114/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mh114/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mh114/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-10T17:45:14Z","updated_at":"2025-10-10T17:45:14Z","